From 4da70d304793d8935b3da6a692080316b74b15f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:02:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] Typer: fixes from the attack on assocsubst,
 abstractstrict and headsubst

- Two selections through the same witness expression unify only if the types of
  the witness unify syntactically (not up to an equality): one requirement
  instantiated at two equal types is two witnesses.
- abstractstrict: selections through the declared witness are atoms of the
  equality procedure.
- assocsubst: the premise witnesses of a conditional conformance are
  substituted into the associated type, as are its type arguments; a
  conformance required by a trait selects the associated type through its own
  witness; bound parameters of a generic requirement are renamed when a
  substituted associated type mentions one of them.
- headsubst: members of extensions are instantiated with the witnesses of the
  extension's requirements; requirements are substituted in order, so that
  chains of projections resolve; the head of a given or of an extension is
  bound to its premises, and a projection through a premise that faces a
  projection through a known witness decides the premise; an elaboration that
  cannot be decomposed makes the projections erroneous instead of opaque.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
